On Thu, 2 Mar 2006, ManaUser wrote:
> Arthur J. O'Dwyer wrote:
>
>>   (3) What should happen when the player polymorphs into a purple worm
>> and digests a monster wearing a ring of foo? Is there any precedent in
>> the code for this situation? (I don't think so. Digesting an "oLS uses
>> it up, and digesting an "oR or speed boots does nothing, AFAICT.)
>> I could make digesting a ring grant the intrinsic, though.
>
> Except for Slow Digestion which would force you to spit the monster out,
> it shouldn't be any different than digesting a monster who is carrying a 
> ring but not wearing it.

   Okay. But notice that in vanilla 3.4.3, monsters /don't/ carry rings
unless they're tame. So this might be a legitimate case of TDTDNTOE
--- why should eating a ring grant the intrinsic if digesting it doesn't?
   On the other hand, at the moment, when you digest a monster, its 
possessions just magically appear on the floor, as if it had carefully
disrobed before entering your gullet. So if the ring is still there on
the floor, obviously you didn't digest it.
   So for now I'll go with your assessment. It seems consistent with
the current state of affairs --- the ring is left on the floor, so it
wasn't eaten, so you don't gain intrinsics from it.

   Good point on Slow Digestion, too. I'll add that to the list of rings
that monsters might want to try on in some cases.

-Arthur


